      "response": "## Investigation report\n\nCitation integrity checked against saved evidence. Human review is required to assess the findings.\n\n### 1. Docs · Low\n\nThe snippet imports the Streamlit library as \\`st\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_57dd72bc887d233f3da8f62ce5172042\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 2. Docs · Low\n\nThe function \\`load\\_rows\\` is decorated with \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_57dd72bc887d233f3da8f62ce5172042\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 3. Docs · Low\n\n\\`load\\_rows\\` returns a list containing the integers 1, 2, and 3\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_57dd72bc887d233f3da8f62ce5172042\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 4. Docs · Low\n\nThe result of \\`load\\_rows\\(\\)\\` is passed to \\`st\\.write\\`, which will display the list in the Streamlit app\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_57dd72bc887d233f3da8f62ce5172042\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### Missing information\n\n- Confirm whether the required credential is configured \\(yes/no\\); provide the provider name, configuration variable names, an endpoint without credentials or secret query parameters, and redacted error messages\\. Do not share credential values or other secrets\\.\n\n### Proposed next steps\n\n- Check whether the \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\` decorator is correctly caching the list so that \\`load\\_rows\\` is executed only once during the app session\\.\n",
